   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "18aa5184",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Part 2: GMOE baseline (Tutel backend)\n",
    "\n",
    "GMOE baseline dùng **Tutel MoE** với top-K routing — chỉ compute top-K experts được chọn per token. Để có ma trận 6×6 giữa **tất cả** experts (yêu cầu cho hình), ta **bypass routing** bằng forward hook + manual einsum.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "1. `forward_pre_hook` capture input của `model.blocks[10].mlp`: shape `(B, 197, D=384)`\n",
    "2. Manually compute output của TẤT CẢ 6 experts bằng `batched_fc1_w`, `batched_fc2_w` từ state_dict\n",
    "3. Lấy **CLS token** (index 0) → `(B, 6, 384)` — giống shape GMOE_Full's output per-image\n",
    "4. Per-sample cosine → average across 4 envs\n",
    "\n",
    "### Fairness & correctness considerations\n",
    "\n",
    "| Aspect | GMOE_Full (Part 1) | GMOE baseline (Part 2) | Impact |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Expert dim | 256 (ExplicitMoEHead) | 384 (DeiT-S FFN) | **Cosine là dim-invariant → không bias** |\n",
    "| Feature level | Post-backbone CLS | MoE layer 10 on CLS | Cùng CLS-level → fair |\n",
    "| Routing | Soft (all 6 always active) | Top-K=2 (bypass via hook) | Model-dependent, không fix được |\n",
    "| Init | Random independent | Pretrained DeiT FFN | Đây **chính là điểm so sánh**, không phải bias |\n",
    "| Dataset | OfficeHome in-split ~3k/env | OfficeHome in-split ~3k/env | Cùng data |\n",
    "| Seeds | seed=0, 4 test envs | seed=0, 4 test envs | Cùng setting |\n",
    "| Aggregation | Per-sample cos → mean | Per-sample cos → mean | Cùng công thức |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Correctness safeguards\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Sanity check einsum**: assert manual-compute output của MoE layer \"span\" output của Tutel (mean best-match cos > 0.90). Nếu einsum sai, output Tutel sẽ không align với bất kỳ manual output nào.\n",
    "- **Matrix invariants**: assert `diag=1.0` và `symmetric` cho mọi matrix.\n",
    "- **Weight layout verified**: layout `(E, hidden, D)` với `fc2_w` TRANSPOSED confirmed từ [vit_helpers.py:336](domainbed/vit_helpers.py#L336)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4ead1591",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "GMOE checkpoint template: /home/hungnt/hungnt/DG-OMOE/multi_dataset/GMOE/OfficeHome/env{env}/seed0/train_output/model.pkl\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# GMOE baseline config\n",
    "GMOE_ALGO_DIR = 'GMOE'\n",
    "GMOE_ALGORITHM_CLASS = 'GMOE'\n",
    "GMOE_CHECKPOINT_TMPL = str(REPO_ROOT / 'multi_dataset' / GMOE_ALGO_DIR / DATASET_NAME / 'env{env}' / f'seed{SEED}' / 'train_output' / 'model.pkl')\n",
    "MOE_LAYER_IDX = 10   # last MoE layer in DeiT-S pattern ['F']*8 + ['S','F']*2\n",
    "\n",
    "print('GMOE checkpoint template:', GMOE_CHECKPOINT_TMPL)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b4b86be4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compute_all_experts_manual(x, fc1_w, fc1_b, fc2_w, fc2_b):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Apply all E experts on all tokens, bypassing Tutel top-k routing.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Tutel Fused MoE weight layout (verified from domainbed/vit_helpers.py:336):\n",
    "        fc1_w: (E, hidden, D)       — same layout as PyTorch Linear(D→hidden).weight\n",
    "        fc2_w: (E, hidden, D)       — stored TRANSPOSED (hidden, D) instead of (D, hidden)\n",
    "        fc1_b: (E, hidden)\n",
    "        fc2_b: (E, D)\n",
    "\n",
    "    x:      (T, D)  input tokens (T = B * n_tokens)\n",
    "    Returns: (T, E, D)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # fc1 (E, hidden, D): y = x @ W.T per-expert → (T, E, hidden)\n",
    "    h = torch.einsum('td,ehd->teh', x, fc1_w) + fc1_b.unsqueeze(0)\n",
    "    h = F.gelu(h)\n",
    "    # fc2 (E, hidden, D): stored permute(0,2,1) → effective W per expert = (hidden, D)\n",
    "    out = torch.einsum('teh,ehd->ted', h, fc2_w) + fc2_b.unsqueeze(0)\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_gmoe_model(ckpt_path, device):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Load GMOE (Tutel) model + return (algo, state_dict).\n",
    "\n",
    "    IMPORTANT: during `algo = algo_class(...)`, the pretrained DeiT weights are loaded\n",
    "    via `model_factory(pretrained=True)`. This prints an `_IncompatibleKeys(...)` message:\n",
    "\n",
    "        missing_keys: blocks.{8,10}.mlp.gates.0.*  +  head.weight/bias\n",
    "\n",
    "    This is BENIGN — those params are (a) NOT in pretrained ImageNet DeiT (MoE gates\n",
    "    were added later; head was dropped due to class mismatch), so they get RANDOM\n",
    "    init, then (b) IMMEDIATELY overwritten by the actual checkpoint load below.\n",
    "\n",
    "    The real checkpoint load uses `strict=True` → any true mismatch raises an error.\n",
    "    Verified: sanity check cell reports mean best-match cos ≈ 0.99, confirming the\n",
    "    checkpoint load is correct (not just structurally compatible, but numerically sound).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    ckpt = torch.load(ckpt_path, map_location=device, weights_only=False)\n",
    "    algo_class = vars(algorithms)['GMOE']\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Suppress the benign pretrained-load print from model_factory\n",
    "    import io, contextlib\n",
    "    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\n",
    "        algo = algo_class(\n",
    "            input_shape=ckpt['model_input_shape'],\n",
    "            num_classes=ckpt['model_num_classes'],\n",
    "            num_domains=ckpt['model_num_domains'],\n",
    "            hparams=ckpt['model_hparams'],\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Real checkpoint load — strict=True raises if anything is missing/unexpected\n",
    "    algo.load_state_dict(ckpt['model_dict'], strict=True)\n",
    "    algo.to(device)\n",
    "    algo.eval()\n",
    "    return algo, ckpt['model_dict']\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def collect_gmoe_baseline_experts(algo, state_dict, loader, device, layer_idx=10):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    forward_pre_hook captures MoE-layer input, then we manually compute\n",
    "    outputs of ALL 6 experts (bypassing top-k routing).\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns: (N, E, D) — CLS token only (matches GMOE_Full's per-image output).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    prefix = f'model.blocks.{layer_idx}.mlp.experts.'\n",
    "    fc1_w = state_dict[prefix + 'batched_fc1_w'].to(device)\n",
    "    fc1_b = state_dict[prefix + 'batched_fc1_bias'].to(device)\n",
    "    fc2_w = state_dict[prefix + 'batched_fc2_w'].to(device)\n",
    "    fc2_b = state_dict[prefix + 'batched_fc2_bias'].to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "    captured = {}\n",
    "    def hook(module, inputs):\n",
    "        captured['x'] = inputs[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    handle = algo.model.blocks[layer_idx].mlp.register_forward_pre_hook(hook)\n",
    "\n",
    "    all_cls_experts = []\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            for x, _y in loader:\n",
    "                x = x.to(device)\n",
    "                _ = algo.predict(x)                                 # triggers the hook\n",
    "                x_in = captured['x']                                # (B, 197, D)\n",
    "                B, T_tok, D = x_in.shape\n",
    "                x_flat = x_in.reshape(B * T_tok, D)\n",
    "                experts_out = compute_all_experts_manual(x_flat, fc1_w, fc1_b, fc2_w, fc2_b)\n",
    "                experts_out = experts_out.reshape(B, T_tok, -1, D)  # (B, 197, E, D)\n",
    "                cls_out = experts_out[:, 0, :, :]                   # (B, E, D) — CLS token\n",
    "                all_cls_experts.append(cls_out.cpu())\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        handle.remove()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return torch.cat(all_cls_experts, dim=0)   # (N, E, D)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9beed039",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WARNING:root:\u001b[31mYou are loading a legacy format of checkpoint with at least one Tutel MoE layer inside, which wouldn't support new Tutel feature allowing the number of experts per checkpoint file to mutate.\u001b[0m\n",
      "WARNING:root:\u001b[31m  The next time you overwrite it with new checkpoint, the recording format will be updated automatically.\u001b[0m\n",
      "WARNING:root:\u001b[31m  However, the new format won't be compatible with early Tutel versions, unless you force loading it with `model.load_state_dict(.., strict=False)`.\u001b[0m\n",
      "WARNING:root:\u001b[31mYou are loading a legacy format of checkpoint with at least one Tutel MoE layer inside, which wouldn't support new Tutel feature allowing the number of experts per checkpoint file to mutate.\u001b[0m\n",
      "WARNING:root:\u001b[31m  The next time you overwrite it with new checkpoint, the recording format will be updated automatically.\u001b[0m\n",
      "WARNING:root:\u001b[31m  However, the new format won't be compatible with early Tutel versions, unless you force loading it with `model.load_state_dict(.., strict=False)`.\u001b[0m\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Sanity check — einsum convention:\n",
      "  x_in  shape:          (4, 197, 384)\n",
      "  y_tutel shape:        (4, 197, 384)\n",
      "  experts_out_all:      (788, 6, 384)\n",
      "  mean best-match cos:  0.9942  (should be > 0.95 if einsum is correct)\n",
      "  min  best-match cos:  0.9731\n",
      "  [OK] einsum matches Tutel output direction\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =========================================================================\n",
    "# SANITY CHECK: verify manual einsum matches Tutel's actual forward\n",
    "# =========================================================================\n",
    "# Tutel fuses top-K routing + expert forward. For the top-K selected experts\n",
    "# on each token, the output should match our manual compute_all_experts_manual\n",
    "# at those indices. If mismatched, the einsum convention is wrong.\n",
    "\n",
    "sanity_ckpt_path = GMOE_CHECKPOINT_TMPL.format(env=TEST_ENVS[0])\n",
    "sanity_algo, sanity_sd = load_gmoe_model(sanity_ckpt_path, device)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Capture both input and output of the MoE layer\n",
    "_cap = {}\n",
    "def _hook_in(module, inputs):\n",
    "    _cap['x_in'] = inputs[0].detach().clone()\n",
    "def _hook_out(module, inputs, output):\n",
    "    # Tutel MoE returns a tensor same shape as input (B, T, D)\n",
    "    _cap['y_tutel'] = output.detach().clone() if torch.is_tensor(output) else output[0].detach().clone()\n",
    "\n",
    "moe_mod = sanity_algo.model.blocks[MOE_LAYER_IDX].mlp\n",
    "h_in = moe_mod.register_forward_pre_hook(_hook_in)\n",
    "h_out = moe_mod.register_forward_hook(_hook_out)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run one small batch\n",
    "sanity_loader = FastDataLoader(dataset=all_in_splits[TEST_ENVS[0]], batch_size=4, num_workers=0)\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    for x, _y in sanity_loader:\n",
    "        _ = sanity_algo.predict(x.to(device))\n",
    "        break\n",
    "h_in.remove(); h_out.remove()\n",
    "\n",
    "x_in = _cap['x_in']                                # (B, 197, D)\n",
    "y_tutel = _cap['y_tutel']                          # (B, 197, D) — Tutel's output (top-K combined)\n",
    "B, T_tok, D = x_in.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "# Manual compute: ALL 6 experts on ALL tokens\n",
    "prefix = f'model.blocks.{MOE_LAYER_IDX}.mlp.experts.'\n",
    "fc1_w = sanity_sd[prefix + 'batched_fc1_w'].to(device)\n",
    "fc1_b = sanity_sd[prefix + 'batched_fc1_bias'].to(device)\n",
    "fc2_w = sanity_sd[prefix + 'batched_fc2_w'].to(device)\n",
    "fc2_b = sanity_sd[prefix + 'batched_fc2_bias'].to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "x_flat = x_in.reshape(B * T_tok, D)\n",
    "experts_out_all = compute_all_experts_manual(x_flat, fc1_w, fc1_b, fc2_w, fc2_b)   # (T, 6, D)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tutel's y_tutel should equal weighted sum of top-K experts. Without access to\n",
    "# gate scores here, we instead verify that for each token, Tutel's output lies\n",
    "# in the span of our 6 expert outputs — specifically, at least one of the 6\n",
    "# manual outputs should be very close (up to scale) to Tutel's output.\n",
    "y_flat = y_tutel.reshape(B * T_tok, D)\n",
    "# cosine between y_tutel[t] and experts_out_all[t, e, :]\n",
    "y_norm = F.normalize(y_flat, dim=-1)                      # (T, D)\n",
    "e_norm = F.normalize(experts_out_all, dim=-1)             # (T, 6, D)\n",
    "cos_y_to_experts = torch.einsum('td,ted->te', y_norm, e_norm)  # (T, 6)\n",
    "\n",
    "max_cos = cos_y_to_experts.max(dim=-1).values              # best-match expert per token\n",
    "mean_best_match = max_cos.mean().item()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Sanity check — einsum convention:')\n",
    "print(f'  x_in  shape:          {tuple(x_in.shape)}')\n",
    "print(f'  y_tutel shape:        {tuple(y_tutel.shape)}')\n",
    "print(f'  experts_out_all:      {tuple(experts_out_all.shape)}')\n",
    "print(f'  mean best-match cos:  {mean_best_match:.4f}  (should be > 0.95 if einsum is correct)')\n",
    "print(f'  min  best-match cos:  {max_cos.min().item():.4f}')\n",
    "assert mean_best_match > 0.90, (\n",
    "    f'Einsum convention mismatch! Tutel output does not align with any '\n",
    "    f'manual-computed expert. Got mean_best_match={mean_best_match:.4f}'\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('  [OK] einsum matches Tutel output direction\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "del sanity_algo, sanity_sd, _cap, experts_out_all, y_tutel\n",
    "torch.cuda.empty_cache()"
   ]
  },
